    "durationMs": 228000,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified. Everything was tested end-to-end against the real PostgreSQL instance:\n\n**Implementation**\n- `src/links/` — `Link` entity (TypeORM), `LinksService` (validation, code generation, atomic `clicks + 1` increment), `LinksController` (`POST/GET /links`, `GET /links/{code}`), `RedirectController` (`GET /r/{code}` → 302)\n- `src/json-error.filter.ts` — global filter making every error a JSON `{error}` body and mapping all bad-request/validation cases (including malformed JSON) to 422\n- `src/migrations/` + `src/migrate.ts` — SQL migration applied by start.sh before serving\n- `src/database/options.ts` — connection parsed from `DATABASE_URL`, nothing hardcoded\n- `start.sh` — applies pending migrations, then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000` (no dependency installs inside)\n- `README.md` — startup section documenting `sh start.sh` and `DATABASE_URL`\n\n**Verified behavior**\n- `POST /links`: 201 `{code, url, clicks: 0}` with URL returned byte-for-byte unchanged; auto-generated 8-char codes from the allowed charset; duplicates → 409\n- Validation → 422: malformed JSON, missing/non-string/relative/ftp/hostless URLs, codes that are too short/long/non-ASCII/non-string\n- `GET /r/{code}`: 302 with exact `Location`, clicks increment exactly once per hit (1, 3, ... confirmed)\n- `GET /links`: creation-order items + total; unknown codes → 404 `{error}`\n- Restart test: clicks and links survived, migration idempotent on second run\n\nTest data was truncated afterward, the server is stopped, and port 8000 is free for the graded run."
  }
